WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.024
Imagine waking up one morning in the
not-too-distant future.

00:00:04.024 --> 00:00:13.841
You open your eyes, and before you even
touch your phone, your AI assistant
already knows that you have a busy day
ahead.

00:00:13.841 --> 00:00:16.210
It has checked your calendar.

00:00:16.210 --> 00:00:20.234
It has looked at the messages that arrived
overnight.

00:00:20.234 --> 00:00:24.672
It has reviewed the documents you were
supposed to read.

00:00:24.672 --> 00:00:29.110
It has noticed that one of your meetings
was moved.

00:00:29.110 --> 00:00:33.134
It has prepared a summary of the important
information.

00:00:33.134 --> 00:00:42.124
And instead of opening ten different
applications, searching through hundreds
of messages, and manually organizing
everything, you simply ask one question.

00:00:42.124 --> 00:00:45.321
“What do I need to know today?”

00:00:45.321 --> 00:00:46.862
Your AI answers.

00:00:46.862 --> 00:00:49.645
Not with a list of notifications.

00:00:49.645 --> 00:00:52.428
Not with a collection of links.

00:00:52.428 --> 00:00:56.038
But with an understanding of what actually
matters.

00:00:56.038 --> 00:00:59.235
It tells you which meeting requires
preparation.

00:00:59.235 --> 00:01:02.845
It tells you which message needs a
response.

00:01:02.845 --> 00:01:07.283
It tells you that a project is falling
behind schedule.

00:01:07.283 --> 00:01:12.549
And perhaps it has already prepared the
first draft of the work.

00:01:12.549 --> 00:01:14.090
You approve it.

00:01:14.090 --> 00:01:16.045
The work gets done.

00:01:16.045 --> 00:01:17.586
This sounds futuristic.

00:01:17.586 --> 00:01:20.783
But pieces of this world already exist.

00:01:20.783 --> 00:01:26.049
And that is what makes the future of
artificial intelligence so interesting.

00:01:26.049 --> 00:01:30.901
We are not simply watching the development
of another software tool.

00:01:30.901 --> 00:01:37.408
We may be watching the beginning of a
completely different way of interacting
with computers.

00:01:37.408 --> 00:01:42.260
For decades, computers have required us to
learn how they work.

00:01:42.260 --> 00:01:43.801
We open applications.

00:01:43.801 --> 00:01:45.342
We navigate menus.

00:01:45.342 --> 00:01:47.297
We search for information.

00:01:47.297 --> 00:01:49.252
We fill in forms.

00:01:49.252 --> 00:01:50.793
We click buttons.

00:01:50.793 --> 00:01:52.334
We move files.

00:01:52.334 --> 00:01:55.944
We copy information from one system into
another.

00:01:55.944 --> 00:02:02.451
Software gives us enormous power, but it
often makes us adapt ourselves to the
software.

00:02:02.451 --> 00:02:05.234
Artificial intelligence introduces a
different possibility.

00:02:05.234 --> 00:02:08.431
What if software could adapt to us?

00:02:08.431 --> 00:02:12.455
What if we could simply describe what we
want?

00:02:12.455 --> 00:02:22.272
Instead of saying, “Open this application,
find this customer, copy this information,
create a report, export it, and send it,”
we could say:

00:02:22.272 --> 00:02:32.089
“Prepare a report showing which customers
are most likely to leave, explain why, and
send the important cases to my team for
review.”

00:02:32.089 --> 00:02:35.286
The computer would figure out the steps.

00:02:35.286 --> 00:02:37.655
That is a profound change.

00:02:37.655 --> 00:02:44.576
Because the real promise of AI is not
merely that machines can generate text or
images.

00:02:44.576 --> 00:02:49.428
The deeper promise is that machines can
begin to understand goals.

00:02:49.428 --> 00:03:06.280
And once a computer can understand a goal,
reason about the steps required to achieve
it, use tools, and evaluate the result,
software starts to look less like a
collection of applications and more like a
collection of intelligent workers.

00:03:06.280 --> 00:03:10.718
This is the beginning of the age of AI
agents.

00:03:10.718 --> 00:03:17.225
But to understand where we are going, we
need to understand where we came from.

00:03:17.225 --> 00:03:23.318
For most of the history of computing,
computers were extremely powerful but
fundamentally literal.

00:03:23.318 --> 00:03:31.066
If you wanted a computer to perform a
task, you had to tell it exactly what to
do.

00:03:31.066 --> 00:03:32.607
Programmers wrote instructions.

00:03:32.607 --> 00:03:34.562
Those instructions became software.

00:03:34.562 --> 00:03:36.103
Software followed rules.

00:03:36.103 --> 00:03:40.541
The computer did not understand the
purpose behind those rules.

00:03:40.541 --> 00:03:42.496
It simply executed them.

00:03:42.496 --> 00:03:44.451
Then came machine learning.

00:03:44.451 --> 00:03:51.785
Instead of programming every rule
manually, we could give machines examples
and allow them to learn patterns.

00:03:51.785 --> 00:03:57.878
This changed fields such as image
recognition, recommendation systems,
speech recognition, and fraud detection.

00:03:57.878 --> 00:04:00.247
Then came modern generative AI.

00:04:00.247 --> 00:04:03.030
Large language models demonstrated
something surprising.

00:04:03.030 --> 00:04:07.468
They could work with language at a
remarkably broad level.

00:04:07.468 --> 00:04:09.423
They could summarize documents.

00:04:09.423 --> 00:04:10.623
Translate languages.

00:04:10.623 --> 00:04:11.823
Write software.

00:04:11.823 --> 00:04:13.364
Explain complicated concepts.

00:04:13.364 --> 00:04:14.564
Generate ideas.

00:04:14.564 --> 00:04:15.764
Analyze information.

00:04:15.764 --> 00:04:17.305
And communicate conversationally.

00:04:17.305 --> 00:04:23.812
Suddenly, the computer was no longer
limited to commands written in a rigid
programming language.

00:04:23.812 --> 00:04:27.836
We could communicate with it using
ordinary human language.

00:04:27.836 --> 00:04:30.619
That alone was a major shift.

00:04:30.619 --> 00:04:34.229
But there was another shift hiding
underneath it.

00:04:34.229 --> 00:04:42.805
If a model can understand a request,
perhaps it can also decide what actions
are necessary to fulfill that request.

00:04:42.805 --> 00:04:45.174
That leads us to agents.

00:04:45.174 --> 00:04:48.784
An AI agent is not simply a chatbot.

00:04:48.784 --> 00:04:55.291
A chatbot waits for you to ask a question
and then gives you an answer.

00:04:55.291 --> 00:04:58.488
An agent can be given a goal.

00:04:58.488 --> 00:05:01.685
It can break that goal into steps.

00:05:01.685 --> 00:05:03.640
It can use tools.

00:05:03.640 --> 00:05:05.595
It can inspect information.

00:05:05.595 --> 00:05:07.550
It can make decisions.

00:05:07.550 --> 00:05:10.333
It can check its own work.

00:05:10.333 --> 00:05:18.909
And it can continue until the task is
complete, within whatever permissions and
boundaries a human or organization gives
it.

00:05:18.909 --> 00:05:20.864
Imagine a sales team.

00:05:20.864 --> 00:05:24.888
Today, a salesperson might spend hours
researching a prospect.

00:05:24.888 --> 00:05:27.671
They look at the company's website.

00:05:27.671 --> 00:05:29.626
They examine previous interactions.

00:05:29.626 --> 00:05:32.823
They check the customer relationship
management system.

00:05:32.823 --> 00:05:34.364
They read emails.

00:05:34.364 --> 00:05:37.147
They search for recent company news.

00:05:37.147 --> 00:05:39.102
They prepare talking points.

00:05:39.102 --> 00:05:41.471
Then they write an email.

00:05:41.471 --> 00:05:47.150
In an AI-native organization, an agent
could perform much of this preparation
automatically.

00:05:47.150 --> 00:05:49.519
It could research the company.

00:05:49.519 --> 00:05:51.474
Understand the account history.

00:05:51.474 --> 00:05:53.015
Identify important changes.

00:05:53.015 --> 00:05:54.556
Suggest a strategy.

00:05:54.556 --> 00:05:56.511
Draft a personalized message.

00:05:56.511 --> 00:06:00.121
And place everything in front of the
salesperson.

00:06:00.121 --> 00:06:03.318
The human still makes the important
decision.

00:06:03.318 --> 00:06:06.928
But the machine handles much of the
preparation.

00:06:06.928 --> 00:06:09.711
Now imagine taking that idea further.

00:06:09.711 --> 00:06:13.735
Suppose the agent is allowed to send the
message.

00:06:13.735 --> 00:06:16.518
Suppose it can schedule a meeting.

00:06:16.518 --> 00:06:19.301
Suppose it can update the CRM.

00:06:19.301 --> 00:06:22.498
Suppose it can monitor the account
afterward.

00:06:22.498 --> 00:06:28.177
Suddenly, we are no longer talking about
AI that helps with one task.

00:06:28.177 --> 00:06:33.443
We are talking about an AI system that
operates an entire workflow.

00:06:33.443 --> 00:06:35.812
This distinction is incredibly important.

00:06:35.812 --> 00:06:39.836
The first wave of AI applications helped
people create.

00:06:39.836 --> 00:06:43.033
The next wave may help organizations
operate.

00:06:43.033 --> 00:06:45.816
That could affect almost every industry.

00:06:45.816 --> 00:06:47.357
Consider software development.

00:06:47.357 --> 00:06:55.933
Today, developers spend time reading
requirements, designing systems, writing
code, debugging, testing, reviewing pull
requests, reading documentation, and
deploying applications.

00:06:55.933 --> 00:06:59.957
AI can already assist with many of these
tasks.

00:06:59.957 --> 00:07:05.636
But the future may involve development
agents that work across an entire
repository.

00:07:05.636 --> 00:07:08.419
A developer could describe a feature.

00:07:08.419 --> 00:07:11.202
The agent could inspect the architecture.

00:07:11.202 --> 00:07:13.157
Identify the relevant files.

00:07:13.157 --> 00:07:14.698
Write the implementation.

00:07:14.698 --> 00:07:15.898
Run tests.

00:07:15.898 --> 00:07:17.098
Investigate failures.

00:07:17.098 --> 00:07:18.298
Make corrections.

00:07:18.298 --> 00:07:19.498
Create documentation.

00:07:19.498 --> 00:07:21.453
Prepare a pull request.

00:07:21.453 --> 00:07:24.236
And then wait for human approval.

00:07:24.236 --> 00:07:27.433
The programmer's role does not necessarily
disappear.

00:07:27.433 --> 00:07:30.216
Instead, the programmer may move upward.

00:07:30.216 --> 00:07:39.206
The important question becomes less about
typing every line of code and more about
architecture, product decisions,
verification, security, and judgment.

00:07:39.206 --> 00:07:42.403
The same transformation could happen in
finance.

00:07:42.403 --> 00:07:46.013
Imagine an AI system monitoring company
finances continuously.

00:07:46.013 --> 00:07:47.554
It sees revenue.

00:07:47.554 --> 00:07:48.754
Expenses.

00:07:48.754 --> 00:07:49.954
Invoices.

00:07:49.954 --> 00:07:51.154
Cash flow.

00:07:51.154 --> 00:07:52.354
Budgets.

00:07:52.354 --> 00:07:53.554
Contracts.

00:07:53.554 --> 00:07:55.509
It notices unusual transactions.

00:07:55.509 --> 00:07:58.292
It compares actual performance with
forecasts.

00:07:58.292 --> 00:08:00.247
It prepares management reports.

00:08:00.247 --> 00:08:03.857
It identifies potential problems before
they become emergencies.

00:08:03.857 --> 00:08:07.054
But again, there is an important
principle.

00:08:07.054 --> 00:08:11.906
The most powerful systems should not
simply be given unlimited authority.

00:08:11.906 --> 00:08:14.689
Financial actions can have serious
consequences.

00:08:14.689 --> 00:08:18.713
So an enterprise AI system may need
permission boundaries.

00:08:18.713 --> 00:08:22.737
Perhaps it can analyze everything but
cannot transfer money.

00:08:22.737 --> 00:08:27.589
Perhaps it can prepare a payment but
requires approval before execution.

00:08:27.589 --> 00:08:34.096
Perhaps low-risk actions can happen
automatically while high-risk actions
require multiple people to approve them.

00:08:34.096 --> 00:08:41.017
This idea of controlled autonomy will
become one of the most important parts of
enterprise AI.

00:08:41.017 --> 00:08:45.455
The future is not necessarily about giving
machines unlimited freedom.

00:08:45.455 --> 00:08:51.134
It is about giving machines the right
amount of freedom for each task.

00:08:51.134 --> 00:08:53.089
Now consider customer support.

00:08:53.089 --> 00:08:57.527
A traditional customer service system
might answer frequently asked questions.

00:08:57.527 --> 00:09:03.206
A more advanced AI agent could understand
the entire history of a customer.

00:09:03.206 --> 00:09:05.575
It could identify the issue.

00:09:05.575 --> 00:09:07.116
Search internal documentation.

00:09:07.116 --> 00:09:09.071
Check the customer's account.

00:09:09.071 --> 00:09:11.440
Determine what actions are permitted.

00:09:11.440 --> 00:09:12.981
Resolve the problem.

00:09:12.981 --> 00:09:14.936
Update the relevant systems.

00:09:14.936 --> 00:09:17.305
And communicate the result naturally.

00:09:17.305 --> 00:09:22.157
If the situation is unusual, it could
escalate to a human.

00:09:22.157 --> 00:09:30.319
The customer might never need to know
whether the first step was performed by a
human or an AI.

00:09:30.319 --> 00:09:34.343
What matters is whether the problem was
solved correctly.

00:09:34.343 --> 00:09:39.609
This brings us to one of the biggest
economic possibilities of AI.

00:09:39.609 --> 00:09:42.806
The cost of intelligence may fall
dramatically.

00:09:42.806 --> 00:09:48.899
Throughout history, highly skilled human
labor has been expensive because human
attention is limited.

00:09:48.899 --> 00:09:52.509
A company cannot instantly hire a thousand
engineers.

00:09:52.509 --> 00:09:55.706
It cannot hire ten thousand analysts
overnight.

00:09:55.706 --> 00:09:59.730
It cannot have a researcher investigate
every possible question.

00:09:59.730 --> 00:10:01.685
Human capacity is constrained.

00:10:01.685 --> 00:10:03.640
AI changes the equation.

00:10:03.640 --> 00:10:09.319
A company might be able to deploy hundreds
or thousands of specialized agents.

00:10:09.319 --> 00:10:11.688
One agent could analyze sales.

00:10:11.688 --> 00:10:13.643
Another could monitor competitors.

00:10:13.643 --> 00:10:15.598
Another could review contracts.

00:10:15.598 --> 00:10:17.553
Another could test software.

00:10:17.553 --> 00:10:19.508
Another could research markets.

00:10:19.508 --> 00:10:21.463
Another could support customers.

00:10:21.463 --> 00:10:23.832
Another could analyze financial data.

00:10:23.832 --> 00:10:26.615
And another could coordinate the others.

00:10:26.615 --> 00:10:31.881
The result could be something that looks
almost like a digital organization.

00:10:31.881 --> 00:10:35.491
This creates an extraordinary opportunity
for small companies.

00:10:35.491 --> 00:10:38.274
Imagine a startup with ten people.

00:10:38.274 --> 00:10:43.953
Historically, competing with a company
employing ten thousand people would be
extremely difficult.

00:10:43.953 --> 00:10:46.736
The larger company has more engineers.

00:10:46.736 --> 00:10:47.936
More salespeople.

00:10:47.936 --> 00:10:49.136
More analysts.

00:10:49.136 --> 00:10:50.677
More support staff.

00:10:50.677 --> 00:10:52.218
More operational capacity.

00:10:52.218 --> 00:10:58.311
But if a small team can multiply its
capabilities using AI, the relationship
changes.

00:10:58.311 --> 00:11:05.232
Ten excellent people supported by
sophisticated AI systems could potentially
operate like a much larger organization.

00:11:05.232 --> 00:11:08.842
That does not mean small companies
automatically win.

00:11:08.842 --> 00:11:11.211
Large companies have advantages too.

00:11:11.211 --> 00:11:12.752
They have data.

00:11:12.752 --> 00:11:13.952
Distribution.

00:11:13.952 --> 00:11:15.152
Capital.

00:11:15.152 --> 00:11:16.352
Brand recognition.

00:11:16.352 --> 00:11:17.552
Customers.

00:11:17.552 --> 00:11:19.093
And existing infrastructure.

00:11:19.093 --> 00:11:24.359
But AI could lower the cost of building
and operating sophisticated businesses.

00:11:24.359 --> 00:11:27.969
That could produce an explosion of new
companies.

00:11:27.969 --> 00:11:32.821
And perhaps the most interesting
businesses will not simply sell AI.

00:11:32.821 --> 00:11:36.845
They will be designed around AI from the
beginning.

00:11:36.845 --> 00:11:45.421
Think about the difference between adding
electricity to an old factory and
designing a factory for electricity from
day one.

00:11:45.421 --> 00:11:50.273
You can take an old process and replace a
few machines.

00:11:50.273 --> 00:11:53.470
Or you can completely redesign the
factory.

00:11:53.470 --> 00:11:56.253
AI-native companies can do the same.

00:11:56.253 --> 00:12:00.277
Instead of asking, “Where can we add a
chatbot?”

00:12:00.277 --> 00:12:01.477
They ask:

00:12:01.477 --> 00:12:07.570
“If intelligent agents are available from
the beginning, how should this company
actually operate?”

00:12:07.570 --> 00:12:10.353
That is a much bigger question.

00:12:10.353 --> 00:12:13.963
Maybe the company has no traditional
operations department.

00:12:13.963 --> 00:12:16.332
Maybe agents handle routine workflows.

00:12:16.332 --> 00:12:20.770
Maybe every employee has a team of
specialized AI assistants.

00:12:20.770 --> 00:12:24.380
Maybe internal information is accessible
through natural language.

00:12:24.380 --> 00:12:28.818
Maybe meetings become less important
because agents continuously coordinate
work.

00:12:28.818 --> 00:12:31.187
Maybe reports are generated automatically.

00:12:31.187 --> 00:12:35.625
Maybe management dashboards are replaced
by conversations with intelligent systems.

00:12:35.625 --> 00:12:39.235
But there is another side to this
transformation.

00:12:39.235 --> 00:12:40.435
Jobs.

00:12:40.435 --> 00:12:46.528
Whenever technology changes the cost of
work, people naturally ask what happens to
employment.

00:12:46.528 --> 00:12:48.897
This question is not new.

00:12:48.897 --> 00:12:50.852
Industrial machines changed agriculture.

00:12:50.852 --> 00:12:52.393
Factories changed manufacturing.

00:12:52.393 --> 00:12:53.934
Computers changed offices.

00:12:53.934 --> 00:12:57.131
The internet changed media, commerce, and
communication.

00:12:57.131 --> 00:13:00.328
AI is different in one important way.

00:13:00.328 --> 00:13:03.938
Previous automation often targeted
physical or repetitive tasks.

00:13:03.938 --> 00:13:06.307
AI can target cognitive tasks.

00:13:06.307 --> 00:13:07.848
It can write.

00:13:07.848 --> 00:13:09.048
Analyze.

00:13:09.048 --> 00:13:10.248
Reason.

00:13:10.248 --> 00:13:11.448
Code.

00:13:11.448 --> 00:13:12.648
Design.

00:13:12.648 --> 00:13:13.848
Research.

00:13:13.848 --> 00:13:15.048
Communicate.

00:13:15.048 --> 00:13:21.141
That means its impact could reach into
professions that previously seemed
protected from automation.

00:13:21.141 --> 00:13:27.234
But there is an important distinction
between automating a task and eliminating
a job.

00:13:27.234 --> 00:13:30.844
A job is usually a collection of tasks.

00:13:30.844 --> 00:13:36.523
AI might automate some of those tasks
while increasing the value of others.

00:13:36.523 --> 00:13:42.202
A lawyer might spend less time searching
documents and more time advising clients.

00:13:42.202 --> 00:13:48.709
A doctor might spend less time on
administrative paperwork and more time
communicating with patients.

00:13:48.709 --> 00:13:54.802
A teacher might spend less time creating
routine materials and more time mentoring
students.

00:13:54.802 --> 00:14:00.895
An engineer might spend less time writing
repetitive code and more time designing
systems.

00:14:00.895 --> 00:14:06.574
A manager might spend less time preparing
reports and more time making decisions.

00:14:06.574 --> 00:14:11.012
So perhaps the future is not simply humans
versus AI.

00:14:11.012 --> 00:14:14.622
It is humans working with increasingly
capable AI.

00:14:14.622 --> 00:14:20.715
The people who learn how to direct these
systems may have a major advantage.

00:14:20.715 --> 00:14:23.498
That leads to an important skill.

00:14:23.498 --> 00:14:28.764
Prompting was one of the early skills
people associated with generative AI.

00:14:28.764 --> 00:14:32.374
But the future skill may be much broader.

00:14:32.374 --> 00:14:34.743
It may be AI orchestration.

00:14:34.743 --> 00:14:37.526
Knowing how to define a goal.

00:14:37.526 --> 00:14:39.481
How to provide context.

00:14:39.481 --> 00:14:41.436
How to establish constraints.

00:14:41.436 --> 00:14:43.391
How to evaluate results.

00:14:43.391 --> 00:14:47.001
How to divide work between humans and
machines.

00:14:47.001 --> 00:14:49.370
How to verify important decisions.

00:14:49.370 --> 00:14:54.636
And how to build systems that remain
reliable when something goes wrong.

00:14:54.636 --> 00:15:00.729
In other words, the future may reward
people who can think clearly about
processes.

00:15:00.729 --> 00:15:08.477
Because if you can describe a process, an
AI system may increasingly be able to
execute that process.

00:15:08.477 --> 00:15:11.260
Now let's move outside the workplace.

00:15:11.260 --> 00:15:12.460
Imagine education.

00:15:12.460 --> 00:15:18.139
A traditional classroom gives many
students the same lesson at the same time.

00:15:18.139 --> 00:15:20.508
But every student is different.

00:15:20.508 --> 00:15:22.049
Some understand quickly.

00:15:22.049 --> 00:15:23.590
Some need repetition.

00:15:23.590 --> 00:15:25.131
Some learn visually.

00:15:25.131 --> 00:15:27.086
Some learn through examples.

00:15:27.086 --> 00:15:29.041
Some need practical exercises.

00:15:29.041 --> 00:15:33.065
An AI tutor could adapt to the individual
student.

00:15:33.065 --> 00:15:36.675
It could explain a concept five different
ways.

00:15:36.675 --> 00:15:39.458
Notice where the student is struggling.

00:15:39.458 --> 00:15:42.241
Generate exercises specifically for that
weakness.

00:15:42.241 --> 00:15:43.782
Adjust the difficulty.

00:15:43.782 --> 00:15:45.323
Provide immediate feedback.

00:15:45.323 --> 00:15:48.520
And remember the student's progress over
time.

00:15:48.520 --> 00:15:52.544
This could make high-quality personalized
education far more accessible.

00:15:52.544 --> 00:15:55.741
But education is not just information
transfer.

00:15:55.741 --> 00:15:57.282
Teachers provide motivation.

00:15:57.282 --> 00:15:58.482
Human connection.

00:15:58.482 --> 00:15:59.682
Judgment.

00:15:59.682 --> 00:16:00.882
Social development.

00:16:00.882 --> 00:16:02.082
And inspiration.

00:16:02.082 --> 00:16:07.761
So again, the most powerful future may
combine machine capability with human
relationships.

00:16:07.761 --> 00:16:09.716
Now imagine personal productivity.

00:16:09.716 --> 00:16:13.326
Today, people often have dozens of small
responsibilities.

00:16:13.326 --> 00:16:14.526
Paying bills.

00:16:14.526 --> 00:16:15.726
Scheduling appointments.

00:16:15.726 --> 00:16:16.926
Managing travel.

00:16:16.926 --> 00:16:18.126
Comparing options.

00:16:18.126 --> 00:16:19.326
Remembering deadlines.

00:16:19.326 --> 00:16:20.867
Responding to messages.

00:16:20.867 --> 00:16:22.067
Finding documents.

00:16:22.067 --> 00:16:23.267
Organizing information.

00:16:23.267 --> 00:16:26.050
Much of modern life is administrative.

00:16:26.050 --> 00:16:28.833
AI agents could reduce this burden.

00:16:28.833 --> 00:16:31.202
You might tell your assistant:

00:16:31.202 --> 00:16:33.571
“I am traveling next month.

00:16:33.571 --> 00:16:34.771
Organize everything.”

00:16:34.771 --> 00:16:37.554
The system could understand your
preferences.

00:16:37.554 --> 00:16:39.095
Find possible flights.

00:16:39.095 --> 00:16:40.295
Compare schedules.

00:16:40.295 --> 00:16:41.495
Check accommodation.

00:16:41.495 --> 00:16:43.036
Build an itinerary.

00:16:43.036 --> 00:16:44.991
Prepare a packing list.

00:16:44.991 --> 00:16:46.532
Identify visa requirements.

00:16:46.532 --> 00:16:50.970
And place the decisions requiring your
approval in one place.

00:16:50.970 --> 00:16:57.477
The experience of using technology becomes
less about operating software and more
about expressing intent.

00:16:57.477 --> 00:17:00.260
That is a major philosophical shift.

00:17:00.260 --> 00:17:04.698
For decades, digital literacy meant
learning how to use computers.

00:17:04.698 --> 00:17:10.791
In the future, digital literacy may mean
learning how to collaborate with
intelligent systems.

00:17:10.791 --> 00:17:13.160
But there are serious risks.

00:17:13.160 --> 00:17:15.529
AI systems can be wrong.

00:17:15.529 --> 00:17:18.312
They can confidently produce incorrect
information.

00:17:18.312 --> 00:17:20.267
They can misunderstand instructions.

00:17:20.267 --> 00:17:23.050
They can use the wrong tool.

00:17:23.050 --> 00:17:27.488
They can expose sensitive information if
systems are poorly designed.

00:17:27.488 --> 00:17:31.926
They can make decisions based on
incomplete or biased data.

00:17:31.926 --> 00:17:38.019
And when AI agents gain the ability to
take actions, errors become more
consequential.

00:17:38.019 --> 00:17:42.457
A chatbot giving you a wrong answer is one
problem.

00:17:42.457 --> 00:17:48.136
An autonomous system sending the wrong
email to thousands of customers is
another.

00:17:48.136 --> 00:17:52.160
An agent making an incorrect financial
transaction is another.

00:17:52.160 --> 00:17:57.426
An AI system modifying production
infrastructure incorrectly could create a
major outage.

00:17:57.426 --> 00:18:00.209
This is why reliability becomes essential.

00:18:00.209 --> 00:18:04.233
Future enterprise AI systems will need
more than intelligence.

00:18:04.233 --> 00:18:06.188
They will need verification.

00:18:06.188 --> 00:18:07.388
Permissions.

00:18:07.388 --> 00:18:08.588
Audit logs.

00:18:08.588 --> 00:18:09.788
Testing.

00:18:09.788 --> 00:18:10.988
Observability.

00:18:10.988 --> 00:18:12.188
Human approval.

00:18:12.188 --> 00:18:13.388
Rollback mechanisms.

00:18:13.388 --> 00:18:14.588
Security controls.

00:18:14.588 --> 00:18:16.129
And clear accountability.

00:18:16.129 --> 00:18:20.567
We should not build systems that simply
say, “Trust me.”

00:18:20.567 --> 00:18:25.005
We should build systems that can show what
they did.

00:18:25.005 --> 00:18:26.960
Why they did it.

00:18:26.960 --> 00:18:28.915
Which information they used.

00:18:28.915 --> 00:18:30.870
Which tools they called.

00:18:30.870 --> 00:18:32.411
What they changed.

00:18:32.411 --> 00:18:35.194
And whether the result was verified.

00:18:35.194 --> 00:18:39.632
That is especially important as AI becomes
integrated into organizations.

00:18:39.632 --> 00:18:43.242
Because an AI agent is not just software.

00:18:43.242 --> 00:18:46.852
It is software that can increasingly make
decisions.

00:18:46.852 --> 00:18:48.807
And decisions require accountability.

00:18:48.807 --> 00:18:51.590
There is another major issue: privacy.

00:18:51.590 --> 00:18:57.683
AI systems may eventually have access to
enormous amounts of personal and
organizational information.

00:18:57.683 --> 00:18:58.883
Your messages.

00:18:58.883 --> 00:19:00.083
Your documents.

00:19:00.083 --> 00:19:01.283
Your calendar.

00:19:01.283 --> 00:19:02.824
Your financial information.

00:19:02.824 --> 00:19:04.024
Your work.

00:19:04.024 --> 00:19:05.224
Your preferences.

00:19:05.224 --> 00:19:06.424
Your conversations.

00:19:06.424 --> 00:19:09.621
This could create extremely useful
personal assistants.

00:19:09.621 --> 00:19:12.404
But it also creates enormous
responsibility.

00:19:12.404 --> 00:19:14.359
Who owns the data?

00:19:14.359 --> 00:19:16.314
Where is it stored?

00:19:16.314 --> 00:19:18.269
Who can access it?

00:19:18.269 --> 00:19:21.879
Can the AI provider use it for training?

00:19:21.879 --> 00:19:25.076
What happens when you leave a company?

00:19:25.076 --> 00:19:28.273
What happens if an account is compromised?

00:19:28.273 --> 00:19:32.297
These questions cannot be treated as minor
technical details.

00:19:32.297 --> 00:19:36.735
They are central to the design of the AI
future.

00:19:36.735 --> 00:19:42.414
Security will become even more important
because AI agents can potentially operate
tools.

00:19:42.414 --> 00:19:48.093
If an attacker compromises an agent, the
problem is not just stolen information.

00:19:48.093 --> 00:19:53.359
The attacker might gain the ability to
make the agent perform actions.

00:19:53.359 --> 00:19:56.556
This creates an entirely new security
model.

00:19:56.556 --> 00:20:00.580
Organizations will need to think carefully
about agent identity.

00:20:00.580 --> 00:20:01.780
Permissions.

00:20:01.780 --> 00:20:02.980
Authentication.

00:20:02.980 --> 00:20:04.180
Tool access.

00:20:04.180 --> 00:20:05.380
Secrets.

00:20:05.380 --> 00:20:06.580
Isolation.

00:20:06.580 --> 00:20:07.780
And monitoring.

00:20:07.780 --> 00:20:12.632
The systems that succeed will not simply
be the most intelligent.

00:20:12.632 --> 00:20:17.070
They will be the systems that combine
intelligence with control.

00:20:17.070 --> 00:20:19.439
Now imagine the competitive landscape.

00:20:19.439 --> 00:20:23.877
Every company will have access to
increasingly capable AI models.

00:20:23.877 --> 00:20:28.315
At first, that might appear to make AI
less valuable.

00:20:28.315 --> 00:20:32.753
If everyone has access to similar models,
what creates differentiation?

00:20:32.753 --> 00:20:36.363
The answer may be everything around the
model.

00:20:36.363 --> 00:20:37.563
Data.

00:20:37.563 --> 00:20:38.763
Workflows.

00:20:38.763 --> 00:20:39.963
Integrations.

00:20:39.963 --> 00:20:41.163
Customer relationships.

00:20:41.163 --> 00:20:42.363
Proprietary processes.

00:20:42.363 --> 00:20:43.563
Distribution.

00:20:43.563 --> 00:20:44.763
Trust.

00:20:44.763 --> 00:20:48.787
And the ability to turn intelligence into
reliable outcomes.

00:20:48.787 --> 00:20:51.570
The model is only one component.

00:20:51.570 --> 00:20:55.594
Imagine two companies using the same
underlying AI model.

00:20:55.594 --> 00:20:58.377
Company A gives employees a chatbot.

00:20:58.377 --> 00:21:05.298
Company B connects the AI to its data,
systems, workflows, permissions,
verification processes, and business
rules.

00:21:05.298 --> 00:21:08.908
Company B can potentially create much more
value.

00:21:08.908 --> 00:21:17.484
This is why the next generation of AI
companies may look less like chatbot
companies and more like infrastructure
companies.

00:21:17.484 --> 00:21:20.267
They will connect intelligence to action.

00:21:20.267 --> 00:21:25.119
That connection is where much of the
economic value could emerge.

00:21:25.119 --> 00:21:27.488
Now let's consider software itself.

00:21:27.488 --> 00:21:31.512
For decades, software has been built as
fixed applications.

00:21:31.512 --> 00:21:35.122
A customer uses the interface the
developer created.

00:21:35.122 --> 00:21:37.905
But what if applications become dynamic?

00:21:37.905 --> 00:21:45.653
Instead of every user seeing exactly the
same interface, the AI could construct an
interface around the task.

00:21:45.653 --> 00:21:50.091
If you need a report, it creates a report
workspace.

00:21:50.091 --> 00:21:54.943
If you need to analyze data, it creates
the appropriate visualizations.

00:21:54.943 --> 00:22:00.209
If you need to manage a project, it builds
a project environment.

00:22:00.209 --> 00:22:03.406
The interface becomes something generated
on demand.

00:22:03.406 --> 00:22:05.775
You don't necessarily navigate software.

00:22:05.775 --> 00:22:08.558
Software navigates the task with you.

00:22:08.558 --> 00:22:12.168
That could make traditional applications
feel very different.

00:22:12.168 --> 00:22:16.606
The operating system itself might become
more conversational and agentic.

00:22:16.606 --> 00:22:21.044
Instead of opening separate programs, you
could describe an objective.

00:22:21.044 --> 00:22:29.206
“Take these photos, organize them by
event, remove duplicates, create an album,
and prepare the best ones for printing.”

00:22:29.206 --> 00:22:31.989
The operating system coordinates the work.

00:22:31.989 --> 00:22:38.082
This is one reason AI agents could become
more important than individual AI
features.

00:22:38.082 --> 00:22:40.865
A feature helps you do something.

00:22:40.865 --> 00:22:44.475
An agent can potentially manage the entire
process.

00:22:44.475 --> 00:22:50.154
And once agents become capable enough, we
may start building teams of agents.

00:22:50.154 --> 00:22:51.695
One agent plans.

00:22:51.695 --> 00:22:52.895
Another researches.

00:22:52.895 --> 00:22:54.095
Another executes.

00:22:54.095 --> 00:22:55.295
Another verifies.

00:22:55.295 --> 00:22:56.495
Another monitors.

00:22:56.495 --> 00:22:58.864
A coordinator manages the workflow.

00:22:58.864 --> 00:23:01.233
This resembles a human organization.

00:23:01.233 --> 00:23:04.016
But there is an important difference.

00:23:04.016 --> 00:23:06.799
Digital agents can potentially communicate
instantly.

00:23:06.799 --> 00:23:08.754
They can operate continuously.

00:23:08.754 --> 00:23:11.951
They can process enormous amounts of
information.

00:23:11.951 --> 00:23:14.734
They do not need to sleep.

00:23:14.734 --> 00:23:16.689
They can be replicated.

00:23:16.689 --> 00:23:18.644
And they can specialize.

00:23:18.644 --> 00:23:21.427
That could make organizations dramatically
faster.

00:23:21.427 --> 00:23:25.451
But speed is not always the same as
progress.

00:23:25.451 --> 00:23:36.510
If an AI system can produce ten thousand
actions per minute, but those actions are
wrong, it is worse than a slow system that
is correct.

00:23:36.510 --> 00:23:42.189
So the future of AI will require a balance
between autonomy and caution.

00:23:42.189 --> 00:23:44.972
Fast systems need strong feedback loops.

00:23:44.972 --> 00:23:47.341
The ability to detect mistakes.

00:23:47.341 --> 00:23:49.296
The ability to stop.

00:23:49.296 --> 00:23:52.493
And the ability to learn from failures.

00:23:52.493 --> 00:23:56.103
This brings us to perhaps the biggest
question.

00:23:56.103 --> 00:23:58.886
What happens when intelligence becomes
abundant?

00:23:58.886 --> 00:24:02.910
For most of human history, intelligence
has been scarce.

00:24:02.910 --> 00:24:06.107
Expertise requires years of education and
experience.

00:24:06.107 --> 00:24:07.648
Research requires time.

00:24:07.648 --> 00:24:09.603
Analysis requires skilled people.

00:24:09.603 --> 00:24:11.144
Writing requires practice.

00:24:11.144 --> 00:24:12.685
Programming requires training.

00:24:12.685 --> 00:24:19.192
If machines can provide increasingly
capable intelligence at extremely low
cost, many activities become cheaper.

00:24:19.192 --> 00:24:24.044
When something becomes cheaper, society
tends to use more of it.

00:24:24.044 --> 00:24:26.827
The same thing happened with computing.

00:24:26.827 --> 00:24:30.437
When computing became cheap, we put
computers everywhere.

00:24:30.437 --> 00:24:33.634
When communication became cheap, we
communicated constantly.

00:24:33.634 --> 00:24:38.072
When information became cheap, we produced
enormous quantities of it.

00:24:38.072 --> 00:24:43.338
If intelligence becomes cheap, we may see
an explosion of intelligence-intensive
activity.

00:24:43.338 --> 00:24:44.538
More research.

00:24:44.538 --> 00:24:45.738
More software.

00:24:45.738 --> 00:24:46.938
More experiments.

00:24:46.938 --> 00:24:48.138
More businesses.

00:24:48.138 --> 00:24:49.679
More personalized education.

00:24:49.679 --> 00:24:51.220
More creative projects.

00:24:51.220 --> 00:24:52.761
More scientific discovery.

00:24:52.761 --> 00:24:53.961
More simulations.

00:24:53.961 --> 00:24:55.161
More analysis.

00:24:55.161 --> 00:25:00.427
This could be one of the most productive
technological transformations in history.

00:25:00.427 --> 00:25:02.796
But abundance also creates noise.

00:25:02.796 --> 00:25:08.062
If everyone can generate unlimited
content, content becomes less valuable by
itself.

00:25:08.062 --> 00:25:12.086
If everyone can create software, software
becomes less differentiated.

00:25:12.086 --> 00:25:16.524
If everyone can produce marketing
material, attention becomes more scarce.

00:25:16.524 --> 00:25:20.134
In such a world, trust becomes extremely
valuable.

00:25:20.134 --> 00:25:21.675
Taste becomes valuable.

00:25:21.675 --> 00:25:23.216
Judgment becomes valuable.

00:25:23.216 --> 00:25:25.171
Original ideas become valuable.

00:25:25.171 --> 00:25:26.712
Relationships become valuable.

00:25:26.712 --> 00:25:31.150
And the ability to distinguish signal from
noise becomes essential.

00:25:31.150 --> 00:25:36.829
Humans may increasingly focus on questions
that machines cannot simply answer through
computation.

00:25:36.829 --> 00:25:38.784
What should we build?

00:25:38.784 --> 00:25:40.739
What is worth pursuing?

00:25:40.739 --> 00:25:43.936
What kind of society do we want?

00:25:43.936 --> 00:25:46.719
What values should guide our systems?

00:25:46.719 --> 00:25:49.088
What should never be automated?

00:25:49.088 --> 00:25:51.871
These are not purely technical questions.

00:25:51.871 --> 00:25:53.826
They are human questions.

00:25:53.826 --> 00:25:59.505
And perhaps that is the most important
point about the future of AI.

00:25:59.505 --> 00:26:04.771
The future will not be determined only by
how intelligent machines become.

00:26:04.771 --> 00:26:10.037
It will be determined by how humans choose
to use that intelligence.

00:26:10.037 --> 00:26:14.061
We can use AI to automate meaningless
administrative work.

00:26:14.061 --> 00:26:18.499
We can use it to help scientists discover
new medicines.

00:26:18.499 --> 00:26:22.523
We can use it to give students
personalized education.

00:26:22.523 --> 00:26:26.547
We can use it to help small businesses
compete.

00:26:26.547 --> 00:26:30.985
We can use it to make software easier to
build.

00:26:30.985 --> 00:26:34.182
We can use it to improve accessibility.

00:26:34.182 --> 00:26:38.620
We can use it to help people communicate
across languages.

00:26:38.620 --> 00:26:41.403
But we can also misuse it.

00:26:41.403 --> 00:26:44.600
We can create systems that invade privacy.

00:26:44.600 --> 00:26:47.797
We can create systems that manipulate
people.

00:26:47.797 --> 00:26:50.166
We can automate bad decisions.

00:26:50.166 --> 00:26:54.604
We can build organizations that become too
dependent on machines.

00:26:54.604 --> 00:26:57.801
So technological progress alone is not
enough.

00:26:57.801 --> 00:26:59.756
We need thoughtful design.

00:26:59.756 --> 00:27:00.956
Good governance.

00:27:00.956 --> 00:27:02.156
Strong security.

00:27:02.156 --> 00:27:03.356
Human oversight.

00:27:03.356 --> 00:27:06.553
And a willingness to question our
assumptions.

00:27:06.553 --> 00:27:13.887
The most successful AI systems may
therefore be those that are not designed
to replace humans everywhere.

00:27:13.887 --> 00:27:17.911
They will be designed to make humans more
capable.

00:27:17.911 --> 00:27:19.866
Think about a scientist.

00:27:19.866 --> 00:27:23.063
The AI can search thousands of papers.

00:27:23.063 --> 00:27:24.263
Generate hypotheses.

00:27:24.263 --> 00:27:25.463
Analyze data.

00:27:25.463 --> 00:27:26.663
Run simulations.

00:27:26.663 --> 00:27:30.687
But the scientist decides which questions
are worth pursuing.

00:27:30.687 --> 00:27:32.642
Think about an entrepreneur.

00:27:32.642 --> 00:27:35.011
The AI can research markets.

00:27:35.011 --> 00:27:36.211
Write prototypes.

00:27:36.211 --> 00:27:37.411
Analyze competitors.

00:27:37.411 --> 00:27:38.611
Prepare presentations.

00:27:38.611 --> 00:27:41.394
But the entrepreneur chooses the problem.

00:27:41.394 --> 00:27:43.349
Think about an engineer.

00:27:43.349 --> 00:27:45.718
The AI can write code.

00:27:45.718 --> 00:27:46.918
Run tests.

00:27:46.918 --> 00:27:48.118
Inspect systems.

00:27:48.118 --> 00:27:52.142
But the engineer remains responsible for
architecture and safety.

00:27:52.142 --> 00:27:54.097
Think about a student.

00:27:54.097 --> 00:27:56.880
The AI can explain a concept.

00:27:56.880 --> 00:27:58.080
Generate examples.

00:27:58.080 --> 00:27:59.280
Create exercises.

00:27:59.280 --> 00:28:02.890
But the student still needs curiosity and
discipline.

00:28:02.890 --> 00:28:06.087
The human remains part of the loop.

00:28:06.087 --> 00:28:10.111
Perhaps the real transformation is not
human versus machine.

00:28:10.111 --> 00:28:12.480
It is human plus machine.

00:28:12.480 --> 00:28:17.746
One person with powerful AI could
accomplish what once required a team.

00:28:17.746 --> 00:28:23.425
One small company could operate at the
scale of a much larger organization.

00:28:23.425 --> 00:28:26.622
One researcher could explore thousands of
possibilities.

00:28:26.622 --> 00:28:30.232
One creator could produce an entire
production pipeline.

00:28:30.232 --> 00:28:34.670
This is why the coming years could be so
interesting.

00:28:34.670 --> 00:28:43.246
We may be entering a period where the
limiting factor is less about access to
information and more about imagination.

00:28:43.246 --> 00:28:46.029
What do you want to create?

00:28:46.029 --> 00:28:49.226
What problem do you want to solve?

00:28:49.226 --> 00:28:52.423
What organization do you want to build?

00:28:52.423 --> 00:28:56.033
What scientific question do you want to
investigate?

00:28:56.033 --> 00:29:00.057
What kind of life do you want to design?

00:29:00.057 --> 00:29:02.840
AI may increasingly provide the
capability.

00:29:02.840 --> 00:29:06.037
Humans still have to provide the
direction.

00:29:06.037 --> 00:29:09.234
And there is something else worth
remembering.

00:29:09.234 --> 00:29:11.603
Technology rarely changes everything
overnight.

00:29:11.603 --> 00:29:13.972
The future usually arrives gradually.

00:29:13.972 --> 00:29:17.996
At first, a new technology seems like a
novelty.

00:29:17.996 --> 00:29:20.779
Then it becomes a useful tool.

00:29:20.779 --> 00:29:22.734
Then it becomes infrastructure.

00:29:22.734 --> 00:29:27.172
Eventually, people stop thinking about it
as technology at all.

00:29:27.172 --> 00:29:29.127
Electricity became invisible
infrastructure.

00:29:29.127 --> 00:29:31.082
The internet became infrastructure.

00:29:31.082 --> 00:29:32.623
Smartphones became infrastructure.

00:29:32.623 --> 00:29:35.406
AI may follow the same path.

00:29:35.406 --> 00:29:39.016
At first, we will talk about using AI.

00:29:39.016 --> 00:29:43.040
Eventually, we may simply expect software
to be intelligent.

00:29:43.040 --> 00:29:47.892
We may be surprised when a system cannot
understand natural language.

00:29:47.892 --> 00:29:54.399
We may be surprised when an application
requires us to manually copy information
between screens.

00:29:54.399 --> 00:29:59.251
We may wonder why a computer cannot simply
complete a task.

00:29:59.251 --> 00:30:04.103
That is when we will know the
transformation has become normal.

00:30:04.103 --> 00:30:08.127
The interface of the future may be
remarkably simple.

00:30:08.127 --> 00:30:10.082
You state an objective.

00:30:10.082 --> 00:30:12.451
The system understands the context.

00:30:12.451 --> 00:30:13.651
It plans.

00:30:13.651 --> 00:30:14.851
It acts.

00:30:14.851 --> 00:30:16.051
It verifies.

00:30:16.051 --> 00:30:18.006
And it reports back.

00:30:18.006 --> 00:30:22.858
Behind that simple experience may be an
enormous amount of technology.

00:30:22.858 --> 00:30:24.058
Models.

00:30:24.058 --> 00:30:25.258
Agents.

00:30:25.258 --> 00:30:26.458
Databases.

00:30:26.458 --> 00:30:27.658
APIs.

00:30:27.658 --> 00:30:28.858
Security systems.

00:30:28.858 --> 00:30:30.058
Workflow engines.

00:30:30.058 --> 00:30:31.258
Memory.

00:30:31.258 --> 00:30:32.458
Monitoring.

00:30:32.458 --> 00:30:33.658
Verification.

00:30:33.658 --> 00:30:38.510
But the user may not need to see any of
it.

00:30:38.510 --> 00:30:49.569
Just as most people do not think about the
servers behind a website, future users may
not think about the AI infrastructure
behind an intelligent assistant.

00:30:49.569 --> 00:30:52.766
They will simply expect things to work.

00:30:52.766 --> 00:30:55.963
And that creates an enormous engineering
challenge.

00:30:55.963 --> 00:31:02.470
Because when software becomes capable of
taking action, reliability becomes more
important than impressive demonstrations.

00:31:02.470 --> 00:31:06.494
A system that writes a beautiful paragraph
is useful.

00:31:06.494 --> 00:31:12.173
A system that safely completes an
important business process is much more
valuable.

00:31:12.173 --> 00:31:14.128
The difference is trust.

00:31:14.128 --> 00:31:19.394
People will trust AI systems when those
systems consistently produce correct
outcomes.

00:31:19.394 --> 00:31:21.763
Not because they sound confident.

00:31:21.763 --> 00:31:24.132
Not because they appear intelligent.

00:31:24.132 --> 00:31:28.984
But because they can be measured, tested,
monitored, and held accountable.

00:31:28.984 --> 00:31:33.836
This is where the next generation of AI
engineering becomes critical.

00:31:33.836 --> 00:31:38.688
The future will require systems that
combine models with deterministic
software.

00:31:38.688 --> 00:31:41.471
AI can reason about ambiguous problems.

00:31:41.471 --> 00:31:44.254
Traditional software can enforce strict
rules.

00:31:44.254 --> 00:31:47.037
Together, they can create powerful
systems.

00:31:47.037 --> 00:31:50.647
The AI can decide what should happen next.

00:31:50.647 --> 00:31:55.085
The software can ensure that certain
actions are never allowed.

00:31:55.085 --> 00:31:58.282
The AI can propose a financial
transaction.

00:31:58.282 --> 00:32:00.651
The system can verify permissions.

00:32:00.651 --> 00:32:03.020
The human can approve it.

00:32:03.020 --> 00:32:05.389
The transaction can be executed.

00:32:05.389 --> 00:32:07.758
Every step can be recorded.

00:32:07.758 --> 00:32:11.782
That combination could become the
foundation of enterprise AI.

00:32:11.782 --> 00:32:14.979
And perhaps, eventually, personal AI as
well.

00:32:14.979 --> 00:32:19.417
Imagine your personal agent five or ten
years from now.

00:32:19.417 --> 00:32:22.200
It does not merely answer questions.

00:32:22.200 --> 00:32:24.155
It knows your goals.

00:32:24.155 --> 00:32:26.110
It understands your preferences.

00:32:26.110 --> 00:32:28.065
It remembers important context.

00:32:28.065 --> 00:32:30.434
It can interact with services.

00:32:30.434 --> 00:32:32.803
It can manage routine tasks.

00:32:32.803 --> 00:32:35.172
It can help you learn.

00:32:35.172 --> 00:32:37.541
It can help you plan.

00:32:37.541 --> 00:32:39.910
It can help you create.

00:32:39.910 --> 00:32:42.693
But ideally, you remain in control.

00:32:42.693 --> 00:32:45.890
You decide what the AI can access.

00:32:45.890 --> 00:32:49.087
You decide what it can do automatically.

00:32:49.087 --> 00:32:51.870
You decide which actions require approval.

00:32:51.870 --> 00:32:54.239
You can inspect its history.

00:32:54.239 --> 00:32:56.194
You can revoke permissions.

00:32:56.194 --> 00:32:58.563
You can replace the system.

00:32:58.563 --> 00:33:02.173
That model of user control will matter
enormously.

00:33:02.173 --> 00:33:08.266
Because the most powerful assistant is not
necessarily the one with the most access.

00:33:08.266 --> 00:33:14.773
It is the one that gives you the greatest
useful capability while preserving your
control.

00:33:14.773 --> 00:33:18.383
So where does all of this leave us?

00:33:18.383 --> 00:33:22.821
We are standing at an unusual moment in
technological history.

00:33:22.821 --> 00:33:27.259
The computer is becoming more capable of
understanding human language.

00:33:27.259 --> 00:33:30.042
It is becoming better at reasoning.

00:33:30.042 --> 00:33:32.825
It is gaining access to tools.

00:33:32.825 --> 00:33:35.608
It is becoming capable of planning.

00:33:35.608 --> 00:33:38.805
And it is beginning to operate workflows.

00:33:38.805 --> 00:33:42.415
The next step is not simply smarter
chatbots.

00:33:42.415 --> 00:33:46.439
It is systems that can turn intentions
into actions.

00:33:46.439 --> 00:33:50.049
That means the way we work may change.

00:33:50.049 --> 00:33:52.832
The way companies operate may change.

00:33:52.832 --> 00:33:56.029
The way software is built may change.

00:33:56.029 --> 00:33:58.812
The way we learn may change.

00:33:58.812 --> 00:34:02.422
The way we interact with computers may
change.

00:34:02.422 --> 00:34:06.032
And perhaps the biggest change will be
psychological.

00:34:06.032 --> 00:34:11.298
For decades, we have thought of computers
as tools that we operate.

00:34:11.298 --> 00:34:16.150
We may soon think of them as collaborators
that we direct.

00:34:16.150 --> 00:34:19.347
That does not mean they become human.

00:34:19.347 --> 00:34:22.130
They will not have our experiences.

00:34:22.130 --> 00:34:26.568
They will not share our lives in the same
way.

00:34:26.568 --> 00:34:31.006
But they may become increasingly capable
partners in intellectual work.

00:34:31.006 --> 00:34:34.616
And that creates a new responsibility for
us.

00:34:34.616 --> 00:34:38.640
We have to learn how to work with them.

00:34:38.640 --> 00:34:42.250
We have to learn how to verify them.

00:34:42.250 --> 00:34:45.033
We have to understand their limitations.

00:34:45.033 --> 00:34:47.402
We have to build safeguards.

00:34:47.402 --> 00:34:53.495
And most importantly, we have to decide
what we want their capabilities to
accomplish.

00:34:53.495 --> 00:34:57.519
Because AI does not automatically create a
better future.

00:34:57.519 --> 00:34:59.060
It creates possibilities.

00:34:59.060 --> 00:35:02.670
Humans choose what to do with those
possibilities.

00:35:02.670 --> 00:35:09.177
The future could be a world where
intelligent systems eliminate enormous
amounts of boring work.

00:35:09.177 --> 00:35:11.960
Where small teams build extraordinary
companies.

00:35:11.960 --> 00:35:14.329
Where students have personalized tutors.

00:35:14.329 --> 00:35:17.112
Where scientists can explore ideas faster.

00:35:17.112 --> 00:35:19.895
Where software becomes easier to create.

00:35:19.895 --> 00:35:24.747
Where people have more time for
creativity, relationships, and meaningful
work.

00:35:24.747 --> 00:35:34.564
Or it could become a world filled with
poorly controlled automation,
misinformation, surveillance, insecurity,
and systems that make decisions people no
longer understand.

00:35:34.564 --> 00:35:39.002
The technology itself does not determine
which future we get.

00:35:39.002 --> 00:35:40.543
Our choices do.

00:35:40.543 --> 00:35:46.636
And perhaps that is why the most important
question about artificial intelligence is
not:

00:35:46.636 --> 00:35:49.005
“How intelligent will machines become?”

00:35:49.005 --> 00:35:51.374
The more important question is:

00:35:51.374 --> 00:35:55.398
“What will we choose to do with that
intelligence?”

00:35:55.398 --> 00:36:02.319
Imagine a world where intelligence is no
longer something you have to access
through a specialist.

00:36:02.319 --> 00:36:04.688
It is available to everyone.

00:36:04.688 --> 00:36:07.885
A student can ask for a tutor.

00:36:07.885 --> 00:36:11.495
A founder can ask for a research team.

00:36:11.495 --> 00:36:15.105
A developer can ask for an engineering
assistant.

00:36:15.105 --> 00:36:18.715
A scientist can ask for a research
partner.

00:36:18.715 --> 00:36:22.325
A designer can ask for a creative
collaborator.

00:36:22.325 --> 00:36:26.763
A small business owner can ask for an
operations team.

00:36:26.763 --> 00:36:29.960
And an ordinary person can simply ask:

00:36:29.960 --> 00:36:32.743
“Help me make sense of this.”

00:36:32.743 --> 00:36:35.526
That world is still being built.

00:36:35.526 --> 00:36:39.964
We do not know exactly what it will look
like.

00:36:39.964 --> 00:36:43.574
We do not know which companies will
succeed.

00:36:43.574 --> 00:36:48.012
We do not know which jobs will change the
most.

00:36:48.012 --> 00:36:52.036
We do not know which AI architectures will
dominate.

00:36:52.036 --> 00:36:56.474
We do not know how quickly these systems
will improve.

00:36:56.474 --> 00:36:59.671
But one thing is becoming increasingly
clear.

00:36:59.671 --> 00:37:10.730
The era of software that simply waits for
instructions is beginning to give way to
software that can understand goals, reason
about problems, and take action.

00:37:10.730 --> 00:37:16.409
And when that happens at scale, artificial
intelligence stops being just another
feature.

00:37:16.409 --> 00:37:17.950
It becomes infrastructure.

00:37:17.950 --> 00:37:21.147
It becomes part of how society operates.

00:37:21.147 --> 00:37:26.826
The biggest opportunity may not belong to
the people who simply use AI.

00:37:26.826 --> 00:37:37.471
It may belong to the people who understand
what becomes possible when AI is connected
to real systems, real data, real
workflows, and real-world decisions.

00:37:37.471 --> 00:37:38.671
The builders.

00:37:38.671 --> 00:37:39.871
The researchers.

00:37:39.871 --> 00:37:41.071
The entrepreneurs.

00:37:41.071 --> 00:37:42.271
The engineers.

00:37:42.271 --> 00:37:43.471
The educators.

00:37:43.471 --> 00:37:44.671
The creators.

00:37:44.671 --> 00:37:50.350
And the people willing to rethink old
processes instead of simply automating
them.

00:37:50.350 --> 00:37:52.719
We are at the beginning.

00:37:52.719 --> 00:38:00.467
The most interesting AI systems of the
future may not look like the AI systems we
use today.

00:38:00.467 --> 00:38:02.422
They may be quieter.

00:38:02.422 --> 00:38:03.622
More integrated.

00:38:03.622 --> 00:38:04.822
More reliable.

00:38:04.822 --> 00:38:06.022
More autonomous.

00:38:06.022 --> 00:38:07.977
And much more useful.

00:38:07.977 --> 00:38:12.001
You may not open an AI application at all.

00:38:12.001 --> 00:38:14.784
You may simply use your computer.

00:38:14.784 --> 00:38:19.222
And behind everything you do, intelligence
may already be there.

00:38:19.222 --> 00:38:22.005
Waiting to understand what you mean.

00:38:22.005 --> 00:38:23.546
Waiting to help.

00:38:23.546 --> 00:38:25.087
Waiting to act.

00:38:25.087 --> 00:38:32.008
And perhaps, for the first time in the
history of computing, the computer will
not ask:

00:38:32.008 --> 00:38:34.377
“What button should I press?”

00:38:34.377 --> 00:38:35.918
It will ask:

00:38:35.918 --> 00:38:38.701
“What are you trying to accomplish?”

00:38:38.701 --> 00:38:40.656
That is the shift.

00:38:40.656 --> 00:38:42.611
From commands to intentions.

00:38:42.611 --> 00:38:44.566
From applications to agents.

00:38:44.566 --> 00:38:48.176
From software that waits to software that
acts.

00:38:48.176 --> 00:38:52.614
From computing as a tool to computing as a
collaborator.

00:38:52.614 --> 00:39:00.776
And if we build it responsibly, the
ultimate goal is not to create a world
where humans become unnecessary.

00:39:00.776 --> 00:39:06.042
It is to create a world where humans can
accomplish far more.

00:39:06.042 --> 00:39:13.376
A world where the limits of what one
person can learn, build, test, and imagine
expand dramatically.

00:39:13.376 --> 00:39:17.814
A world where technology does not simply
save us seconds.

00:39:17.814 --> 00:39:20.183
It gives us back time.

00:39:20.183 --> 00:39:22.966
It does not simply automate work.

00:39:22.966 --> 00:39:24.507
It expands capability.

00:39:24.507 --> 00:39:27.704
And it does not replace human ambition.

00:39:27.704 --> 00:39:32.556
It gives that ambition a much more
powerful set of tools.

00:39:32.556 --> 00:39:36.994
The future of AI is therefore not only
about machines.

00:39:36.994 --> 00:39:38.949
It is about us.

00:39:38.949 --> 00:39:42.559
It is about what we choose to build.

00:39:42.559 --> 00:39:44.928
What we choose to automate.

00:39:44.928 --> 00:39:47.297
What we choose to protect.

00:39:47.297 --> 00:39:50.907
And what we choose to remain uniquely
human.

00:39:50.907 --> 00:39:52.862
The technology is arriving.

00:39:52.862 --> 00:39:56.059
The question is what we do next.

00:39:56.059 --> 00:39:59.369
And that future is closer than it looks.
